    <channel>
        <title>DuoUpdater</title>
        <!--
          The Sparkle feed. `scripts/publish-release.sh` regenerates this file on
          every release and pushes it here. The app reads it through
          https://updates.duoupdater.app/appcast.xml (workers/appcast relays this
          file); builds before that read
          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/main/appcast.xml
          directly, so this path must keep working.

          Deliberately empty rather than absent: an appcast with no items means
          "nothing newer available", which Sparkle handles as up-to-date, whereas
          a missing file is a fetch error on every check. The first release fills
          it in.

          Release history starts here. Earlier builds were published from a
          separate binary-only repo that existed only while the source was
          private, and are not carried over.
        -->
        <item>
            <title>0.5.10</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:47:29 +0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/releases/tag/v0.5.10</link>
            <sparkle:version>128</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.10</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Surge and TablePlus no longer offer an update your licence won't open.** Both apps refuse to run a version released after your updates ended; that version now shows a lock instead of an update button, and the lock says when your coverage ended and to renew in the app.

**A major upgrade can keep a backup just this once.** With backups turned off, the confirmation before a major upgrade now offers "Back Up & Update", and its "Settings" link opens the backup setting directly.

**More apps get the right runtime badge.** iPhone and iPad apps built with React Native, and apps built with GPUI, egui, Wails or PyQt (shown as Qt), used to show "iOS App", Native or no badge.
]]></description>
